# Guards, Meta & Lazy Loading

## One guard, one authority

```ts
router.beforeEach(async (to) => {
  const lessons = useLessonsStore()
  await lessons.ensureLoaded()               // single-flight bootstrap
  if (typeof to.meta.track === 'string') {
    const mod = lessons.findModule(to.meta.track, String(to.params.module))
    if (mod && useProgressStore().isModuleLocked(mod.id)) {
      return { name: 'dashboard', query: { blocked: mod.id } }
    }
  }
  if (to.name === 'capstone' && !useProgressStore().capstoneUnlocked) {
    return { name: 'dashboard' }
  }
  return true
})
```

The guard **asks the unlock service** — it contains zero curriculum rules.
Business logic lives in stores/engine; guards only translate decisions into
redirects. Duplicating checks inside components is a smell (drift + double
sources of truth).

## Meta as declarative config

```ts
{ path: '/settings', meta: { title: 'Settings', requiresBoot: false } }
document.title = to.meta.title ?? 'Rust Mastery'
```

## Route-level code splitting

```ts
every view except Dashboard: component: () => import('./views/X.vue')
```

Each page becomes its own chunk; first paint ships only the dashboard. Monaco
is further isolated via manualChunks so it downloads once, cached.

